WEBVTT

00:00:10,030 --> 00:00:14,670
I'm getting ready to submit a second cheek swab for supplement recommendations.

00:00:14,670 --> 00:00:19,070
How does one know what it might be a good time to do a rife update?

00:00:20,510 --> 00:00:25,470
But almost a year, but faithfully using it, but doing well, but my PSA is recently going up.

00:00:26,670 --> 00:00:36,190
So it depends on the cancer. So for prostate cancer, really the only time you need to do a rife

00:00:36,190 --> 00:00:45,070
update for prostate cancer is if there's metastasis. So if there's no metastasis with prostate cancer,

00:00:45,070 --> 00:00:49,630
with other cancers, it depends. If the person's getting worse, it's good to check that rife

00:00:49,630 --> 00:00:55,630
update. They don't check and see if you need a rife update. They don't do it. So a lot of you

00:00:55,630 --> 00:01:02,030
send in your cheek swab forms and you check general recommendations. You might make some notes and you

00:01:02,030 --> 00:01:07,710
might check rife update too and you don't need a rife update. So we don't charge you for a rife

00:01:07,710 --> 00:01:16,670
update. So you could check that and I'll check most likely the answers. No, you won't need it.

